# Drafted by Gemini (R11c lottery), edited.

~ start
lottery_stranger [smile]: Step right up and try the Founder's Round draw. Every slip in this hat holds a fair chance at a brighter season.
Narrator: His grey coat is brushed clean, and the paper slips in his upturned hat rustle like dry leaves.
* What is the grand prize? -> prize
* What are the terms of the draw? -> terms
* Buy a slip for ten gold -> draw
* Look closer at his open ledger -> ledger
* Decline the offer and walk on -> refuse

~ prize
lottery_stranger [smile]: One hundred gold coins in a leather purse, paid on the spot, plus a full year of effortless good fortune.
-> start

~ terms
lottery_stranger [neutral]: Ten gold coins a draw. If you do not win, we simply cross your name from the active roll.
lottery_stranger [sly]: Nobody in Wickermoor complains of a bad draw, I promise you that.
-> start

~ ledger
lottery_stranger [neutral]: Ah, a love for tidy bookkeeping. I record every name in clean black ink to prevent disputes.
* [Insight DC 14] Read the names in the ledger -> ledger_read | ledger_fail
* [Intimidation DC 15] Tear the ledger out of his hands -> tear | ledger_fail
* Step away -> start

~ ledger_read
Narrator: Dozens of local names are struck through in wet black ink. Passing townsfolk look right past those cottages as if no one ever lived there.
-> start

~ ledger_fail
lottery_stranger [smile]: Forgive me, friend, the damp air smudges the ink if I leave the pages open too long.
Narrator: He shuts the leather cover with a soft, polite thump and tucks the brass clasp into place.
-> start

~ tear
Narrator: The ledger bindings snap in your grip, scattering inked pages across the mud.
lottery_stranger [smile]: That is one way to balance an account. Enjoy your evening in Wickermoor, travellers.
Narrator: He steps back between two lantern-bearers, and when the smoke clears, his grey coat is gone.
set wm_lottery_done
set wm_lottery_broken
-> END

~ draw
lottery_stranger [smile]: Ten gold received, and recorded in full. Reach into the hat whenever you are ready.
gold -10
check Charisma DC 12 -> win | lose

~ win
lottery_stranger [smile]: Look at that mark upon the paper. We have ourselves a fortunate soul tonight.
Narrator: Villagers clap and cheer too brightly, smiles stretched tight in the lantern glow.
gold +100
set wm_lottery_done
-> END

~ lose
lottery_stranger [neutral]: A blank slip, I am afraid. Let me tidy the register before you go.
Narrator: His nib draws a cold black line through your name, and the air turns chill and thin.
set wm_lottery_done
-> END

~ refuse
lottery_stranger [smile]: Your privilege, travellers. Should you feel luckier on another turn of the clock, you know where I stand.
Narrator: He touches the brim of his hat with two gloved fingers and turns back to the crowd.
set wm_lottery_done
-> END
